CSS selector JIT for ARMv7 (Thumb-2)

The selector compiler is only enabled for x86_64 and ARM64, so 32-bit ARM matches every selector in
the C++ SelectorChecker: a third of the main thread during a Wikipedia load on the LG C1. This adds
the ARMv7 register set (r0-r3 caller-saved, r4 r5 r8-r11 callee-saved; r6 and ip belong to the
MacroAssembler, r7 is the frame pointer), saves r6 and lr/r7 around the compiled function, keeps
sp 8-byte aligned at helper calls, uses SDIV for :nth-child modulo (so the JIT is on only when the build targets a core with
hardware divide, e.g. -mcpu=cortex-a55), and leaves selectors that need
more than the 10 available registers to the C++ checker.

